[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axis derivation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Public entry points (`grep -rE '^[A-Za-z_].*\(' c_src/include/`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | entry point | level | notes |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `helloworld()` | **lowest level == only level** | there is no convenience wrapper and no lower-level function beneath it; this single symbol *is* the full public API |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Runtime options / modes / flags: **none.** There is no init function, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m context struct, no setter, no global variable, no environment lookup
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`getenv` appears 0 times in the C), and 0 `if`/`switch`/`#ifdef` branches.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Compile-time variants: **none** (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` section, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `CMakeLists.txt` defines no options).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the C code's behaviour cannot be varied by *arguments*. What it *does*
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m interact with is the one piece of external state it touches: the libc
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stdout` `FILE` stream, via `printf`. That makes the real configuration axes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Invocation count** — 0 / 1 / many (statelessness; the C keeps no state,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    so output must be exactly N repetitions).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **`stdout` buffering mode** — fully buffered, line buffered, unbuffered
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`setvbuf`). `printf` behaves differently in each; a translation that wrote
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    through a *different* buffer (e.g. `std::io::stdout()`) would diverge here.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **`stdout` destination shape** — regular file vs. pipe. libc picks the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    default buffering from `isatty`, so the destination changes the code path.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. **Interleaving with caller-side stdio** — the caller emits its own
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `printf`/`fwrite` before/after/between calls. This is the composed-pipeline
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    case: it detects buffer mismatch and out-of-order flushing, which
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    per-call tests cannot see.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. **Interleaving C and Rust implementations in one stream** — C, Rust, C,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Rust… into a single fd, checking the merged byte stream.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. **Concurrency** — N threads calling simultaneously.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7. **Call-shape / ABI variation on the valid path** — because the declaration
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `int helloworld();` is unprototyped, a valid C caller may invoke it through
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    pointers of several arities. (Invalid *values* are `ERRORS.md`; here the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    concern is that the arity itself is a shape the ABI distinguishes.)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Randomization (fixed seed `0x5EED_C0FFEE`, SplitMix64) supplies the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m per-row varying quantities: repetition counts, thread counts, buffer sizes,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and the caller-side interleaved payload bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
